  "changes": [
    "Adds Crystal Candyworks as an independent third area after Gelato completion, with a one-time 1500-coin entry and twelve authored Crystal boards. Developer area switching and test wallets include Crystal.",
    "Crystal launches candy along straight finger-directed trajectories at constant speed without gravity. The preview stops at the first target or wall; bounded collision stepping, finite ball lifetimes and clear-drain handling belong to Crystal.",
    "A timed Prism pickup duplicates live balls while preserving their spent-special, lifetime and cooldown state. The optional Second Prism upgrade costs900 coins, requires tray6 and Power4, and adds a second scheduled offer without resetting Power.",
    "A Crystal-specific three-spire upgrade map uses all62 sequential family/tier identities and an always-visible Second Prism tile. Seven original native PNGs provide candy atlases, equipment, tray, room, journey and upgrade courtyard art through bounded per-key UV metadata.",
    "Profile envelope5 adds independent Crystal ownership. Crystal checkpoints use schema5 with exact offer/Prism state; Bakery and Gelato keep schema4 captures and unchanged gameplay fingerprints. Existing maps, Gelato node ownership and earlier area economies remain."
  ],
  "update_compatibility": "Same Android preview package and signing identity as v0.6.14 with code25. Install over the preview to retain package-private app data. The loader accepts profile versions1 through5 and writes version5; Crystal has independent money, upgrades and Second Prism ownership. Crystal active runs use schema5; Bakery/Gelato captures remain schema4, with their content fingerprints unchanged and legacy checkpoint decoding preserved. An older preview does not understand profile5 and must not overwrite it through ordinary autosave. Physical Android installation remains for user testing.",
